WEBVTT

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:11.490
The battle of the spirits rises up to the sky,

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:21.770
as the ivy's vivid colors seethe in jade-colored eyes.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:31.800
The flower-columns reveal a hundred forms,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:41.430
as the outcome reveals distinct truths and falsehoods.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:47.020
Chapter Nine

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:47.020
Fire Whirlwind

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.210
I first met you three years ago, didn't I?

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:00.760
What's the noise on the other side of that door?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.010
That's the sound of pigeons.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:05.430
What's the buzzing noise on the other side of that door?

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.810
That's the sound of a snake swallowing a frog.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.770
What's the noise on the other side of that door?

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:14.310
That's the sound of parents killing their children with hammers.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.280
What's the noise on the other side of that door?

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.940
What do you think happened?

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.940
That's the sound of a dog gnawing a cat to death.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.940
Go fetch the surveillance camera's footage.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.490
Are you alive?

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.200
Hey, are you alive?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.630
Please tell me: are you alive?

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:36.210
Be quiet or I'll be forced to kill you.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.920
Well then...

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.800
am I alive?

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.390
What a crazy old screwball.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.470
You're the crazy one.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.220
You're already dead.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.020
Think carefully. Why are you here?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.690
You must have died in battle.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:58.980
You're spouting nonsense.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.360
I'm obviously alive.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.280
Then, show me some proof.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.200
Proof?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.160
Proof that you're alive.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.250
If you're alive, you should be able to die, right?

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.290
I am...

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.460
alive.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.920
Then, you should be able to die.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.090
Go on, show me.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.670
Prove that you're alive.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.720
Prove...

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.550
that I'm alive...

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.370
Go on, do it.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.720
If you're alive, you can die.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.730
I am...

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.940
alive.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:37.190
Go on! Go on! Go on!

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.360
That's why...

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.440
I can die...

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.740
Go on, show me you can die!

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.640
When an oxcart stops moving,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.310
do you blame the oxen,

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.560
or do you blame the cart?!

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.280
What–

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.990
Do you blame the oxen or the cart?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.530
Answer me!

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.000
Kurumazo.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:39.000
You kill anyone who doesn't give you a satisfactory answer.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.170
I doubt anyone could converse with a man like you.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.260
However...

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.090
You've done it again?

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:51.890
Kagetsu.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.060
What's your answer?

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:59.770
When an oxcart stops moving, do you blame the oxen or the cart?

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.570
That's not even worth thinking about.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.820
You run the cart over the cow.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:15.660
That's a good one.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.500
You're a pretty amusing woman.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.300
After that, Kagetsu became the yin to your yang.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.380
Moving as one, unable to leave each other's side.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:31.640
And yet...

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:42.810
Kagetsu is no longer here. She's been killed.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.320
By Kuro!

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.570
I have come here today to get an answer from you.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.870
I expect a good answer.

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:58.540
You're alone in a field when Kuro sneaks up behind you.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:02.250
Do you kill him by <i>pulverizing</i> him into meat paste?

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.960
Or do you kill him by <i>grinding</i> his bones into dust?

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.880
Which is it?

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.140
Neither.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:18.680
I will <i>crush</i> his soul into pieces to such an extent that he'll never be reincarnated.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:24.310
Then, I will <i>dump</i> the pieces into a cesspit.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.940
Superb answer.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.700
Do whatever you wish, but return with his head.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:32.860
Sir!

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:48.130
What is this?

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.550
You don't know what a bike is?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:51.800
Bike?

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.430
It's a machine you ride.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:58.350
But it requires practice, so not everyone can ride one.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.350
In the past, you needed a license to ride one.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.980
Everyone, listen up.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.610
We're almost at the Red Castle...

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:11.610
To learn the truth, we cannot fail in our mission.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:15.820
For the sake of our fallen comrades, Saniwa and Izana.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.910
In any case, to boost morale, we must have...

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:22.290
meat and potato hotpot.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:26.960
Hotpot...

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.260
It's ready.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.970
Kuon, aren't you gonna eat?

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.180
I'm fine, thanks.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.100
Um...

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:47.730
Don't tell me... I should have used the sukiyaki soup instead?!

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:48.860
But, you know...

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:52.780
It's true that people are attracted to the taste of sukiyaki soup because of its many charms...

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:57.130
However, in my opinion, potatoes can only work with pork!

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.990
No, that's not the issue at all.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.120
Is this really the right time for this?

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.000
Are you worried?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.710
The enemy won't wait for us.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.090
Ah, so that's what you're on about.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.460
If that's the problem, the bridge is only lowered once a day.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.510
We won't make it at this point.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:17.390
We'll spend the rest of today here and wait till dawn.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.600
Still, even with that exc–

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:19.600
Delicious.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.360
It's delicious.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.990
That route will probably work,

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:42.790
but do you know which direction the Red Army will be coming from?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.290
Considering all the territory they control,

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.870
it'll get difficult from Yokohama onwards.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.960
We have no choice but to close our eyes and charge through.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.300
You don't sound particularly confident.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:55.170
"With my awesome driving skills,

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.930
I can <i>vroom</i> to anywhere."

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.180
What the hell...

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.590
You don't know it?

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:01.550
It's from Falcon Rock.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.350
I used to watch it all the time.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.020
It's an anime from my childhood.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:07.520
I loved it.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.520
The father's name was Condor Jumbo.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:10.520
Yes, yes, that's right!

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.860
The title of the movie version was "Monaco Survival."

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.610
Right, right, right!

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.740
So, which areas do they control?

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:19.110
That topic again?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.620
Could you please explain everything to me?

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.120
It's a long story.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.880
Have you heard of the Yamato Group?

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:42.350
Before the Great Disaster, they were quite an influential company.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:46.890
Steel, ships, real estate, construction, electronics, machinery, automobiles and so on...

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:50.100
Their ventures into various industries were always successful.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.520
However, the Red Army was lurking in the shadows.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:59.070
The Great Disaster gave them the opportunity to rapidly expand their area of control.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.160
Using the SDF as their military power base,

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.910
they gained supremacy over Kantou,

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.750
and created their own kingdom.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:11.960
Tokyo is now completely silent under their control.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:24.510
I wonder what will happen when we step into their domain.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:27.560
Well, once you start complaining, you'll find more and more to complain about.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.940
My thought process is a simple one.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.110
I will definitely infiltrate the enemy to see Kuromitsu again.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:38.440
And when I do...

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.030
all shall be revealed.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:35.120
What's going on?!

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:38.290
Damn it!

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:42.800
We've been discovered already...

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.090
It's almost like they knew Kuro was coming.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:46.590
Another one's coming.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.770
We'll be done for if it carries on like this!

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.100
A tunnel!

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:11.700
That saved us.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.810
But what should we do? If it carries on like this...

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:17.120
I shall act as bait.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.750
Lend me your bike.

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:21.000
We'll take different roads.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.920
That's absurd!

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:24.130
I will be fine.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:26.300
It is probably no harder than riding a horse.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.560
Kuro, show me your ear.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:37.730
Sorry. It's a communications device.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.230
We're almost at the exit.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:51.950
Here they come!

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.090
Kuro, can you hear me?

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.930
We'll meet up somewhere after the third bridge.

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:11.810
Keep going straight.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:12.560
Understood.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.400
The road will get smoother once we reach the Yoga Promenade!

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.020
Until then, hold on tight!

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.800
I guess I have to finish them off now...

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:08.940
The road's getting smoother!

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.780
Now, Kuon!

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:06.340
The fool who is not afraid of the sword.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.380
The fool who is not afraid of death.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:13.470
The fool who is not afraid of me.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:16.720
The fool who is not afraid of my master.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.810
I shall not be satisfied until I kill you, Kuro!

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:31.070
Kuro has escaped my grasp.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:35.820
But leave your head behind; I shall bathe it in my urine!

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:46.880
Kuro!

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.300
We'll meet up soon!

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.270
Kuro's in!

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.030
All right!

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:25.540
We're leaving Kasumigaseki.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:28.000
The Red Castle's already in view.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:37.010
There's not much time before the drawbridge lowers.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:38.640
We have to make it.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:26.020
Damn it!

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:27.780
HQ, do you read?

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:28.940
We've detected intruders.

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:31.150
Intercept them!

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:32.320
Headquarters receiving.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:34.190
We'll send our forces out to eliminate them.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.490
Don't even consider escaping!

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:48.580
He's like a Kasha!

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:58.490
Karuta, we can't continue like this!

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.430
It's fine. Leave it to me!

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:11.520
Raise the drawbridge quickly!

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:12.480
Now!

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:14.110
Seal the entrance as well!

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:18.110
The bridge is...

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:28.750
Are you alive or are you dead?

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:39.050
I can't give up now!

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:53.980
"W-With...

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:02.280
With... my awesome driving skills,

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:07.160
I can <i>vroom</i> to anywhere."

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:09.760
Karuta!

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.270
Are you alive?

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:17.810
Please tell me: are you alive?

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:20.480
Karuta, Kuro is–

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:22.070
Karuta!

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:29.330
You're already dead.

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.880
H-How?!

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:44.170
I make no distinction between being alive and being dead.

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:58.060
Karuta...

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:28.170
Next Chapter

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:28.170
The Castle
of Illusion
